   "file": "about.md",
   "heading": "about",
   "text": "I am a recent MSc graduate in AI for Engineering and Design from the University of Bath, with a background in Computer Systems Engineering. I am interested in building AI and software systems that solve practical problems, particularly where machine learning meets engineering.\n\nMy academic work has involved machine learning, signal processing, feature engineering, and working with real-world data. For my master's dissertation, I explored how information from amplitude signals could be used to improve phase signals in wearable pulmonary monitoring, combining signal processing techniques with machine learning experiments.\n\nI enjoy understanding how things work beneath the surface, testing ideas, and measuring whether a solution actually improves on what came before. I am particularly interested in the practical side of AI: not just building a model, but understanding its limitations and evaluating its performance.\n\nI am based in London, UK, and I am looking for an opportunity in AI engineering, machine learning, or software engineering where I can keep learning, take on meaningful technical challenges, and contribute to building useful systems.",
