   "file": "experience.md",
   "heading": "MSc Artificial Intelligence for Engineering and Design, University of Bath (2024 to 2026)",
   "text": "MSc Artificial Intelligence for Engineering and Design, University of Bath (2024 to 2026). My master's degree focused on applying artificial intelligence and machine learning to engineering problems. Through academic projects, I worked with data processing, feature engineering, signal processing and machine learning models, developing an understanding of how to turn raw data into something that can be analysed and evaluated.\n\nFor my dissertation, *Dual Modality Pulmonary Imaging for Bedside Monitoring Using AI*, I explored how amplitude and phase signals collected during breathing could be used to support pulmonary monitoring Amplitude signals provided clearer breathing patterns, while phase signals were noisier. I investigated signal-processing techniques to enhance phase information using amplitude-derived information, then compared machine learning approaches to evaluate the results.\n\nThe project taught me to approach technical problems systematically: understand the data, establish a baseline, test different approaches and evaluate whether an improvement is meaningful rather than assuming a more complex method is automatically better.",
