   "file": "projects.md",
   "heading": "News Classification Evaluator and Ground Truth",
   "text": "News Classification Evaluator and Ground Truth. I evaluated an AI system that classifies news articles into four categories: World, Sports, Business, and Sci/Tech. I manually labelled 30 articles, compared my labels with the AI's predictions and the benchmark labels, and analysed where the classifications disagreed.\n\nThe AI achieved 80% accuracy against the benchmark, with a Cohen's kappa of 0.7329. I examined the confusion matrix, confidence calibration, prompt engineering, and the limitations of accuracy on imbalanced datasets. For example, a classifier that predicted World for every article could still achieve 80% accuracy because World dominated the dataset, despite failing to recognise the other categories.\n\nThis project helped me understand the importance of evaluating AI systems with multiple metrics, investigating errors, and questioning whether a headline performance figure tells the whole story.",
