   "file": "projects.md",
   "heading": "Weed Classification Using Deep Convolutional Neural Networks",
   "text": "Weed Classification Using Deep Convolutional Neural Networks. An image-classification project focused on identifying 25 plant and weed species from a dataset of 15,050 images. I developed and evaluated a modified VGG16 convolutional neural network using Python, TensorFlow and Keras.\n\nI conducted eight structured experiments across different model and dataset configurations, analysing accuracy, F1-score, confusion matrices and training and validation behaviour. Across five runs, the model achieved an average accuracy of 97.92%, with a standard deviation of 0.005. Using a reduced dataset also lowered average runtime by approximately 30% while maintaining accuracy above 95%.\n\nThis project gave me practical experience with computer vision, deep learning, experimental design and model evaluation.\n\nStack: Python, TensorFlow, Keras, VGG16, computer vision.",
